<p>The United States and Gulf Arab states are pushing for United Nations action to reopen the Strait of Hormuz after intelligence assessments warned that Iran is unlikely to ease its restrictions on the waterway soon. Because the strait carries roughly one-fifth of global oil and gas trade, the standoff has become not just a regional security crisis but a global energy and shipping concern. At the UN Security Council, Bahrain has circulated multiple drafts of a resolution backed by the United States that would authorize countries to use &quot;all defensive means&quot; to secure maritime transit for at least six months. But the vote has been postponed as Russia and China continue to object to key language. Iran has warned that the effort would be provocative, while reporting from several outlets says Tehran sees its hold on the strait as one of its few remaining sources of leverage over Washington.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/KLTXso4e7WhvTxyJiHSflCcXinDdDWAZBsjQSDNEn5c1jeUjB_cIc53irfwcSLRSGGFt8NhccGK1ztEqULSkubGHLnwdighObZVk_s-9Wihz' alt='Members of the United Nations Security Council vote on a draft resolution during a meeting on the situation in the Middle East at the United Nations headquarters on March 11, 2026 in New York City.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Draft softened: Earlier versions referenced Chapter VII of the UN Charter, but negotiators removed that language after objections from China, Russia and France in an effort to win broader support.</li><li>Council delays: Diplomats told reporters the Security Council vote first moved from Thursday to Friday, then to Saturday, with The Hindu reporting it was later pushed to sometime next week.</li><li>GCC initiative: The push to reopen the strait comes from Gulf Cooperation Council states — Saudi Arabia, the UAE, Qatar, Kuwait, Oman and Bahrain — acting through Bahrain, the council&#x27;s current president.</li><li>Use of force: The latest draft would let states act in the strait and adjacent waters using defensive measures they judge necessary and proportionate to keep navigation open.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>United States intelligence officials: Recent intelligence assessments say Iran is unlikely to reopen the strait soon because control of the passage gives Tehran leverage over the United States and helps keep energy prices high. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/04/exclusive-us-intelligence-warns-iran-unlikely-ease-hormuz-strait-chokehold-soon'>Al-Monitor</a>)</li><li>Bahrain and Gulf Arab states: Bahrain, backed by Gulf Cooperation Council members and the United States, has kept revising the Security Council resolution and lobbying for support to protect shipping through the waterway. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1988384/unsc-divided-as-gulf-pushes-to-reopen-hormuz'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Russia and China: Both governments have objected to core wording in the draft resolution, especially provisions authorizing defensive action, and have helped delay a council vote. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/bahrain-postpones-vote-on-un-resolution-aimed-at-ending-irans-stranglehold-on-strait-of-hormuz/article70821402.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>Iran: Iran has warned that the Security Council effort would be provocative, underscoring its opposition to outside-backed moves to change the current situation in the strait. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1988384/unsc-divided-as-gulf-pushes-to-reopen-hormuz'>Dawn</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/iran-unlikely-to-ease-hormuz-strait-chokehold-soon-report-11309150#publisher=newsstand'>Iran Unlikely To Ease Hormuz Strait Chokehold Soon: Report</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/us-intelligence-warns-iran-unlikely-to-ease-hormuz-strait-chokehold-soon-sources-say'>US intelligence warns Iran unlikely to ease Hormuz Strait chokehold soon: Sources</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1988384/unsc-divided-as-gulf-pushes-to-reopen-hormuz'>UNSC divided as Gulf pushes to reopen Hormuz</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/bahrain-postpones-vote-on-un-resolution-aimed-at-ending-irans-stranglehold-on-strait-of-hormuz/article70821402.ece'>Bahrain postpones vote on UN resolution aimed at ending Iran&#x27;s stranglehold on Strait of Hormuz</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/04/exclusive-us-intelligence-warns-iran-unlikely-ease-hormuz-strait-chokehold-soon'>Exclusive-US intelligence warns Iran unlikely to ease Hormuz Strait chokehold soon, sources say</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/video/inside-story/2026/4/3/will-force-be-used-to-reopen-strait-of-hormuz'>Will force be used to reopen Strait of Hormuz?</a> - aljazeera.com</li></ul>